==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{qualifier|alternative spelling}} [[ass backwards]], [[ass-backward]], [[ass backward]]
* [[back-asswards]], [[bass-ackwards]]

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{context|colloquial}} Oriented [[backwards]], particularly after a [[mishap]].
#: ''The car spun out of control and I ended up '''ass-backwards''' in a ditch.''
# {{context|idiomatic|colloquial}} Hopelessly [[misguided]]; having taken the utterly wrong choice.
#: ''No wonder it doesn't work.  The whole design is '''ass-backwards'''.''

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{context|colloquial}} Moving backwards, that is, [[rear end]] first.
# {{context|idiomatic|colloquial}} In a hopelessly misguided manner.
#: ''They did the whole design '''ass-backwards'''.  No wonder it doesn't work.''

